# Build inputs for OpenStack 2026.1 Gazpacho on Rocky Linux 10.2 — every one pinned.
#
# This is the TARGET: the same OpenStack release the Ubuntu 26.04 shell gets
# from its distribution archive. epoxy.manifest (2025.1) is kept beside it as a
# research record and is NOT the deliverable.
#
# There is no `gazpacho-rdo` distgit branch and no centos10-gazpacho repository:
# `epoxy-rdo` is the newest release branch RDO has, and `centos10-master` is the
# only trunk tree. So the packaging here is RDO's `rpm-master` spec — the only
# one that exists for anything newer than 2025.1 — pinned to an exact commit and
# pointed at the released 2026.1 tarball.
#
# Two consequences, both handled by build-rpms.sh rather than by hand:
#   * `rpm-master` specs ship `Version: XXX` / `Release: XXX` for DLRN to fill
#     in, so this file carries the version and release.
#   * A master spec does not always match a released tarball. Where it does not,
#     the fix is a reviewable patch in ./spec-patches, not an inline sed.
#
# Versions are the FINAL 2026.1 releases, read from
# openstack/releases deliverables/gazpacho/*.yaml on 2026-09-28; every one has a
# stable/2026.1 branch upstream. Commits from `git ls-remote`, same day.
#
#
# OpenStack release signing keys this manifest trusts, pinned by sha256. The
# spec names the one it wants in %global sources_gpg_sign; a key the manifest
# does not list stops the build.
# 2026.1 is signed by TWO keys: glance and placement were released 2026-04,
# keystone/neutron/nova/horizon are 2026-09 point releases made after OpenStack
# rotated its cycle key. The fingerprints were read out of each .asc and matched
# against the key files published at releases.openstack.org/_static/.
KEY 0x30566c450e41d7c91e442dfb231f942f608ddeff 0f7901e358e78067604188563264589ee3a53f2369379a9b6310ab698af10fc9
KEY 0xb8e9315f48553ec5aff9ffe5e69d97da9efb5aff fcbacfaef9b9b915a417d02f78be95fbaaebcaefa58c32e279e73f2ee2ccbfe6
#
# fields: package  distgit-repo  distgit-commit  spec-file  version  release  tarball  tarball-sha256  url-project  signing-key
#
